  "state_summary": "Round 3, seed 157. The packet reports 429 observed records, 2,901 eligible candidates, no pending experiments and no validation/test records. The supplied molecule, condition, candidate and observed tables were considered together. Recent measurements strengthen molecule-specific response hypotheses and reveal substantial errors for m205 and m107. Learning opportunities now include testing whether those errors persist across conditions and transfer to related structures, while resolving the remaining m125 loading-solvent interaction. Expected learning value is inferred; the feedback does not establish overall Row accuracy after retraining.",
  "important_observations": [
    "[Observed measurements] The m125 2/1 factorial now separates some previously confounded effects. At 100 µl sample volume, increasing DCM loading-solvent volume from 300 to 500 µl changes V1/V2 from 15.408/29.583 to 6.975/56.858 ml (c8d43713db33bf820a1d, 69b09343d0b9995c3ae4). At 150 µl sample volume, the same solvent-volume change gives 13.725/31.375 to 32.950/69.808 ml (19f19f196ba5787a01b0, facbcedbecb46072b04c). V2 increases in both contrasts, while V1 moves in opposite directions. This supports a condition interaction, not one common endpoint shift.",
    "[Observed measurements] m125 at 2/1 with 500 µl DCM has nonmonotonic V1 across 50, 100 and 150 µl sample volumes: 36.233, 6.975 and 32.950 ml; V2 is 63.992, 56.858 and 69.808 ml (cc2a23d8eb9de61d2ab3, 69b09343d0b9995c3ae4, facbcedbecb46072b04c). Its 5/1, 300 µl DCM series is much more stable: V1 approximately 42.3–43.0 and V2 69.7–74.0 ml across the same sample-volume range (780b13846ace50ede763, 74cf50c6ec476a394b01, 549daca56bed1c9d2bcc). A pervasive large loading effect is therefore unsupported. Variability or missing covariates remain competing explanations for the unusual 2/1 V1 pattern.",
    "[Observed measurements and historical predictions] m205, a primary naphthylethanol, measured 51.433/98.375 ml at 5/1, 100 µl sample, DCM 400 µl; its premeasurement prediction missed by -38.289/-71.708 ml (48853fd78c77153b963a). m107, a donor-free ether-containing beta-ketoester, measured 43.200/101.442 ml at 5/1, 50 µl sample, DCM 300 µl, with errors -16.470/-54.335 ml (c6924324ddd95f249df6). These distinct structures both expose serious local errors; donor count alone cannot explain them.",
    "[Observed measurements] Increasing sample volume from 50 to 100 µl advances V1 at m160 5/1 by 4.142 ml, m161 5/1 by 7.583 ml and m216 10/1 by 7.617 ml. Their V2 changes are approximately -2.775, -1.650 and +0.133 ml, respectively (ad833f34f6b91872362d, b4e0e9dc92fca2c88b90, a60552f4d1a5ced4641f, 17902fa9c7f8ea9b456e, e47aebe2660b9e1528de, 9cd02352c2ed7a3e2321). m90 at 5/1 also has progressively earlier V1 with increasing sample volume, but V2 has a minimum at the middle volume (29db30571b2a1ae59cc7, 855832bd4005ac7abdc6, b51b5dbcd2a38b174973). Loading effects are endpoint- and molecule-dependent.",
    "[Observed measurements] m92 with EA loading solvent has V2 29.625 ml at 20/1 and 61.950 ml at 50/1 at fixed 100 µl sample and 200 µl loading solvent (8b58e9d7a710f55e49d3, 7b42519983cf93dd7efd). Its 50/1, 50 µl measurement also has a long interval, 14.883/58.542 ml (7caf1db075b91197ba34). The high-ratio V2 response survives lower loading; these points do not establish whether the intervening curve is smooth or contains a transition.",
    "[Observed measurements] The new m167 100 µl points fit its established V2 response: 4.417/12.233 ml at 2/1 and 4.658/16.075 ml at 5/1 (ea6260d7052cabfca181, 34a133db8364fd665ae6). At both ratios, V1 changes substantially from 50 to 100 µl but little from 100 to 150 µl. This refines the loading hypothesis toward a locally saturating response. The 0/1, 50 µl result is 3.708/11.767 ml (e947f47c9e991c7add4c). These are coherent condition observations, not independent replicate evidence.",
    "[Observed measurements] H8 gains direct ratio-response evidence: m212 at fixed 100 µl sample increases from 22.067/37.183 ml at 5/1 to 46.675/78.067 ml at 10/1 (252c027cf5a42b92c953, 70cba7a21b5a01fb8e73). m31 at fixed 50 µl increases from 13.008/32.283 to 31.500/67.275 ml over the same ratios (156594686f5cf7182bcc, b3d9bb5afa82b99f2a11). Steep responses occur in both a secondary amine and a donor-free nitrile/ketone.",
    "[Observed-table correction] 7e327de3d5f5fcab9a7e is m123 at 2/1, 50 µl sample, DCM 400 µl, measuring 6.583/9.425 ml. It is not m117 at 20/1. The previous rationale therefore did not acquire the proposed donor-rich m117 measurement. No m117 measurement appears in the supplied observed table."
